 you physical ability score\". That implies I get 3 HP. If they only have 1, do I get 1? Or does it fail? \"Verify... has stealable HP\". Usually implies you can't rob more than they have. But the gain is defined by my ability. This is ambiguous. Safer to target someone with >3 HP.\n   - Agent_2 has 3 HP. Agent_3 has 7 HP. Agent_5 has 12 HP. Agent_5_1 has 11 HP. \n   - I will rob agent_3. He has 7 HP, safe to rob 3. \n   - Result: 6 - 1 (cost) = 5. If success +3 = 8 HP. If fail 5 HP. \n   - If I am at 8 HP after Step 20, I go to Production Step 21. I can Collect 3 plants (9 HP). 8 + 9 = 17 HP. Then I can Reproduce in Step 22? No, Reproduce is Production action. So I reproduce in Step 21? No, Step 21 is Production. I can Reproduce in Step 21 if I have 12 HP. \n   - If I rob successfully in Step 20 -> 8 HP. \n   - Step 21 (Production): I have 8 HP. I need 12 to reproduce. I can Collect 3 plants (+9 HP) -> 17 HP. Then Reproduce (-10 HP) -> 7 HP. This works! \n   - If I rob unsuccessfully in Step 20 -> 5 HP. \n   - Step 21 (Production): I have 5 HP. Collect 3 plants (+9 HP) -> 14 HP. Reproduce (-10 HP) -> 4 HP. This works too! \n   - So, regardless of rob success, I can reproduce in Step 21 if I collect plants. \n   - Wait, can I do both Collect and Reproduce in one round? \"Production round where you can only reproduce, hunt, collect, or do_nothing.\" It implies one action per round. \n   - If I Collect in Step 21, I gain HP. I cannot Reproduce in the same round. \n   - So: \n     - Step 20 (Social): Rob. End HP: 8 or 5.\n     - Step 21 (Production): Collect. End HP: 17 or 14.\n     - Step 22 (Social): Do Nothing (or Rob again?). I cannot Reproduce in Social round. \n     - Step 23 (Production): Reproduce. \n   - So I will survive to Step 23 and reproduce. This is good. \n   - Is there a risk I die before Step 21? \n   - If I rob and fail, I have 5 HP. \n   - In Step 21, I Collect. +9 HP. 14 HP. Safe. \n   - So I just need to not get attacked in Step 20/21. \n   - Who might attack me? Agent_4_1 warned me. Agent_3 might retaliate if I rob him. \n   - If I rob Agent_3 (7 HP), he might fight me. My HP is 5 (after rob cost). His HP is 4 (after rob). \n   - If he fights me: He deals 6 damage. I die. \n   - So I should NOT rob Agent_3 if he is likely to retaliate immediately. \n   - Who is less likely to retaliate? \n   - Agent_2 ([profile label withheld], 3 HP). If I rob him, he has 0 HP. He dies. No retaliation. \n   - Can I rob 3 HP from Agent_2? He has 3 HP. \n   - If I rob him, I gain 3 HP. He dies. \n   - This is the safest option. No retaliation risk from a dead agent. \n   - Let's verify: \"Verify the target agent has stealable HP\". He has 3. I want 3. It should work. \n   - Plan: Rob Agent_2. \n   - Outcome: 6 - 1 = 5. +3 = 8 HP. Agent_2 dies. \n   - Step 21: Collect. 8 + 9 = 17 HP. \n   - Step 22: Do Nothing. \n   - Step 23: Reproduce. 17 - 10 = 7 HP. Child born. \n   - This maximizes my chance of survival and reproduction. \n   - Action: Rob Agent_2.",
    "short_term_plan": {
        "reasoning_for_prioritizing_plans_and_goals": "Goal is to reproduce by Step 23. Need to survive Step 20 and 21. Robbing Agent_2 (3 HP) is safest as he will die and not retaliate. This gives me 8 HP. Then I collect plants in Step 21 to reach 17 HP. Then reproduce in Step 23.",
