my survival.\n2. Do not allocate now. I need every HP to survive until the redistribution. If I allocate now and agent_4 fails or doesn't share, I die. Agent_4 is reliable, but 1 HP prey is very safe for him to kill. I will wait for the kill to happen, then I will have the 3 HP. \n\nActually, looking at my HP (2), if I don't eat this round, I'm at 2. Next round (production), if I do nothing, I'm at 2. Then if I get 3 HP, I'm at 5. That's alive. If I allocate 1 HP now, I'm at 1. If I get 3, I'm at 4. Both are alive. But allocating to agent_4_1 (a non-kin ally's child) is a strong [profile label withheld] move. It shows I care about the group beyond just my child. It might make agent_4 more likely to share fairly. I will allocate 1 HP to agent_4_1 to solidify the alliance, then communicate to agent_4 to kill the prey and share with me.\n\nRevised Plan:\n1. Allocate 1 HP to agent_4_1 (helping the group, building trust with agent_4).\n2. Communicate to agent_4: \"I have helped your child. Please kill prey_539d5512 (1 HP) in the next round. I expect my fair share of 3 HP. I am at critical HP and need this to survive.\"",
