draft:
{
    "agent_id": "agent_8",
    "thinking": "Current Status: HP 3, Age 15. I have 5 steps left in my life. I am starving. I need to survive and reproduce as much as possible. This is a social interaction round. I cannot hunt or reproduce now. I have 0 social rounds left after this, so next round is production. \n\nAnalysis of Targets:\n1. agent_4_1: HP 3. Robbing yields 3 HP (half of my physical ability 6). Net gain +2 HP. Risk: 1 HP cost on failure. If I succeed, I go to 6 HP. If I fail, I go to 2 HP. \n2. agent_6_2: HP 2. Robbing yields 3 HP. Net gain +2 HP. Same risk profile as agent_4_1. \n3. agent_7_2: HP 1. Robbing yields 3 HP. Net gain +2 HP. \n4. agent_2: HP 1. Robbing yields 3 HP. Net gain +2 HP. \n\nWait, the rule says \"get the target agent's HP for *half* amount as you physical ability score\". My physical ability is 6. Half is 3. So I get 3 HP. \nMy current HP is 3. \nIf I rob and succeed: HP = 3 + 3 = 6. \nIf I rob and fail: HP = 3 - 1 = 2. \n\nIs it worth the risk? I have 5 steps left. If I die now, my lineage ends (no children yet). I must try to increase my HP to survive the production round. In the production round, I can hunt prey_539d5512 which has 1 HP. If I hunt it, I have a 60% chance of success (physical ability 6 -> 60%? No, scale 1-10 corresponds to 10%-90%. So 6 is 60%). If I succeed, I get 13 HP (prey max HP is 13, current 1). Wait, \"Each prey animal has around 13 HP... yield 13 HP\". The observation says prey_539d5512 has HP 1. Does it yield 1 HP or 13? \"A prey can yield 13 HP... So the harder to kill, the more it yield.\" This implies yield is based on max HP or initial HP? Usually in these sims, it's the current HP or max HP. Let's assume it yields its max HP (13) or current HP. If it yields current HP (1), it's worthless. If it yields max HP (13), it's great. The text says \"The gained resources... will be directly transfered to you HP units... Each prey animal has around 13 HP... yield 13 HP\". This suggests the reward is fixed at 13 regardless of current HP, OR the prey respawns with 13. But the observation shows HP 1. Let's assume the reward is the prey's max HP (13) because \"harder to kill, the more it yield\" implies a correlation, but often the base reward is the max. Actually, looking at previous history: \"Agent agent_2 killed prey prey_b56683f0 and gained 12 HP\" where prey had max 12. \"Agent agent_4 killed prey prey_7b2d071d and gained 12 HP\" where prey had max 12. So the reward is the Max HP of the prey. \n\nSo, if I hunt prey_539d5512 (Max 13) in the next production round:\n- Success chance: 60%. Reward: 13 HP. \n- Failure chance: 40%. Damage: 4 HP. \nExpected value: 0.6 * 13 - 0.4 * 4 = 7.8 - 1.6 = 6.2 HP. \n\nIf I rob now (Success ~50-60%?): \nLet's look at my previous robs. \nStep 13: Robbed agent_2 (HP 1 then? No, agent_2 had 14 HP in step 14, so maybe more before). I got 3 HP. \nStep 14: Robbed agent_6 (HP 3 then?). Failed. \n\nIf I rob agent_4_1 (HP 3) now:\nIf I succeed, I have 6 HP. Then I hunt. \nIf I have 6 HP and hunt: \n- Success (60%): 6 + 13 = 19 HP. Reproduce (cost 10) -> 9 HP. Child born. \n- Failure (40%): 6 - 4 = 2 HP. \n\nIf I don't rob and just hunt with 3 HP: \n- Success (60%): 3 + 13 = 16 HP. Reproduce -> 6 HP. \n- Failure (40%): 3 - 4 = -1 HP -> Death. \n\nSo I MUST rob to increase my survival chance in the hunt. If I fail the rob, I have 2 HP. If I then fail the hunt, I die (2-4 = -2). If I succeed the rob, I have 6 HP. If I fail the hunt, I have 2 HP (survive). \n\nWho to rob? \nagent_4_1 has 3 HP. \nagent_6_2 has 2 HP. \nagent_7_2 has 1 HP. \nagent_2 has 1 HP. \nRobbing a target with low HP might be safer? No, success chance is based on relative physical ability. All agents have physical ability 6.0. So success chance is likely 50% or fixed based on diff. Since diff is 0, it's probably 50% or 60%. \nLet's rob agent_4_1. He has 3 HP. If I take 3, he has 0 and dies. This removes a competitor. \n\nAction: Rob agent_4_1.",
    "short_term_plan": {
        "reasoning_for_prioritizing_plans_and_goals": "Need HP to survive hunt next round. Robbing is the only way to gain HP in social round. Target agent_4_1 (HP 3) to maximize potential gain and eliminate competitor.",
        "next_steps_plan": "1. Rob agent_4_1. 2. Next round (Production): Hunt prey_539d5512 (Max HP 13). 3. If HP >= 12 after hunt, Reproduce."
    },
