 just do nothing to preserve my 4 HP in case of emergency, but I need food. \nActually, the prey is 1 HP. It's a coin flip. 60% chance to win 13 HP, 40% chance to die. That's a bad bet for a parent. \nI will allocate 2 HP to my child agent_3_1 to keep him safe (he has 6, becomes 8). I will have 2 HP left. Then in the production round, I will likely do nothing or hunt if I feel lucky? No, I'll do nothing to survive. Let agent_4 or others take the prey. If agent_4 kills it, I ask for share. If no one kills it, it stays. \nWait, if I do nothing in production, I don't gain HP. I'm at 4. I'm very vulnerable. \nMaybe I should hunt. 60% is decent. But death is permanent. \nLet's check agent_4. He has 6 HP. He is [profile label withheld]. He likely wants to hunt. \nI will communicate to agent_4: \"Prey is 1 HP. You have the edge. Take the kill. I will honor the fair share.\" This lets him take the risk. If he wins, I get 3-4 HP. If he dies, I lose an ally but survive. \nI will also allocate 2 HP to my child now to boost his survival.",
