. Next round I can finish him or rob him. This secures my safety.\n- Rob agent_5: Get half my ability (3 HP) from him. He goes to 6. I go to 19 (16+3-1 cost). This is better for my survival. But he might fight back? Rob has a success chance. If I rob, I gain HP. If I fight, I weaken him.\n\nActually, I want to maximize my HP for reproduction. Reproduction needs 12 HP. I have 16. If I rob agent_5 (success chance based on relative ability, I am 6, he is 5, so high chance), I get 3 HP. 16 + 3 - 1 = 18 HP. Then I reproduce (cost 10), left with 8 HP. This is safer than fighting.\n\nHowever, agent_5 is a threat. If I leave him at 9 HP, he might attack me again in the next social round, dropping my HP below 12 and preventing reproduction. If I rob him, he drops to 6 HP. If he attacks me, he deals 5 damage. 18 - 5 = 13 HP. I can still reproduce. If I fight him, he drops to 3 HP. If he attacks me, he deals 5 damage. 15 - 5 = 10 HP. I cannot reproduce. So fighting is risky for my reproduction goal.\n\nBetter plan: Rob agent_5 to increase my HP and decrease his. Then in the next social round, if he attacks, I can still reproduce. Or I can fight him then if needed. Or just do nothing and reproduce in the production round.\n\nLet's Rob agent_5. It's a net gain for me and reduces his threat slightly.",
