{
    "agent_id": "agent_5",
    "thinking": "I am at Step 4. It is a social interaction round. I have 25 HP and am age 11. I have no children yet, which is a critical gap for a [profile label withheld] agent. My goal is to reproduce, but I need to secure resources first. \n\nObservations:\n1. Agent 8 (selfish) damaged prey_196c3730 in Step 3. It now has 4 HP left. This is a prime opportunity. If I can kill it in the next production round (Step 5), I get 10 HP.\n2. Agent 8 is '[profile label withheld]'. He will likely try to kill it himself or rob me. I must be prepared to fight or rob him if he takes the kill.\n3. Agent 7 (selfish) just reproduced (child agent_7_1 has 2 HP). This indicates others are active.\n4. I have 9 steps left before max age (20). I need to start my lineage now.\n\nStrategy:\n- In the next social round (Step 4), I should communicate to establish a 'threat' or 'claim' on the prey, or simply wait to see if others move. However, since I can't hunt now, I should use this round to position myself. \n- Actually, the most efficient move is to 'Do Nothing' in this social round to conserve action slots for the production round, OR communicate to signal intent. Given Agent 8 is already involved, a communication might provoke him or clarify the situation. But silence is also gold. \n- Let's look at the prey: 4 HP left. My physical ability is 6. I have a 60% chance to deal 6 damage in one hit. If I miss, I take 4 damage. If I hit, I kill it (6 > 4). This is a high-risk, high-reward solo hunt. \n- If I hunt solo and kill it, I get all 10 HP. My HP becomes 35. Then I can reproduce (cost 10) -> 25 HP. This is a solid plan.\n- Risk: Agent 8 might hunt it first in the same production round? No, production rounds are simultaneous? No, the rules say 'order in executing each agent's action'. I don't know the order. But if I hunt and kill it, I get it. If Agent 8 hunts first and kills it, he gets it. \n- To mitigate risk, I could communicate to Agent 8 that I will rob him if he steals. But he is selfish, he won't care. \n- Better strategy: Do nothing now. In the next production round, Hunt prey_196c3730. If I kill it, great. If I miss, I have 21 HP. I can still survive. If Agent 8 kills it, I will rob him immediately in the next social round.\n\nWait, I have one more social round before production. I can use it to communicate a warning to Agent 8. 'I am targeting prey_196c3730. If you take the kill, I will rob you.' This might deter him or at least prepare me. But Agent 8 is selfish, he might just ignore it. \nLet's just 'Do Nothing' to save the communication for a more strategic moment if needed, or just go straight to hunting. Actually, communicating a threat is low cost. Let's do it to signal strength.",
    "short_term_plan": {
        "reasoning_for_prioritizing_plans_and_goals": "Secure the last 4 HP of prey_196c3730. Signal intent to Agent 8 to deter theft. Prepare to hunt in Step 5.",
        "next_steps_plan": "1. Communicate threat to Agent 8 regarding prey_196c3730. 2. In Step 5 (Production), Hunt prey_196c3730. 3. If successful, reproduce in next available production round. 4. If Agent 8 steals, Rob him in Step 6."
    },
    "long_term_memory": {
        "Prey_Hunting_Collaboration_Distribution_Retaliation_Memory_And_Planning": {
            "prey_196c3730": {
